.page hexdump 1 display a file in hexadecimal and ASCII

# SYNOPSIS
*hexdump* [*-C*] [_FILE_]

# DESCRIPTION
`hexdump` shows the bytes of _FILE_ (or standard input) in the canonical layout: the offset in hexadecimal, sixteen bytes as hexadecimal numbers in two groups of eight, and the same bytes as characters between bars, with unprintable bytes shown as a dot. A last line gives the total length.

Runs of identical sixteen-byte lines are replaced by a single `*`.

# OPTIONS
@ *-C*
    The canonical layout. It is the only layout there is, so the option changes nothing; it is accepted because everyone types it.

# EXAMPLES
    hexdump -C /bin/hello | head
    echo "gensokyo" | hexdump -C

# SEE ALSO
xxd(1), od(1), strings(1)
